{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/thm-unital-groebner-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:unital-groebner-decomposition","kind":"theorem","title":"Free module decomposition via unital Gröbner--Shirshov bases","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-admissible-system","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-groebner-basis","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-remainder-module"],"proofs":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prf-unital-groebner-decomposition"],"tags":["groebner-basis","free-module","decomposition"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition","text":"main-theorem.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/main-theorem.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:unital-groebner-decomposition\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a commutative ring with unity. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> be an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra\nwhich is free as an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module and without quasi-zeros. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> be\nan <a href=\"#def:admissible-system\">admissible system</a> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code> be a\ntwo-sided ideal of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> with a unital\n<a href=\"#def:groebner-basis\">Gröbner--Shirshov basis</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code>. Define <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde{O}(G)</code> to be\nthe <a href=\"#def:remainder-module\">free <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module</a> spanned by the monomials\nwhich do not occur as leading monomials of members of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code>. Then, as free\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-modules,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">A/I \\;\\cong\\; \\tilde{O}(G) \\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad A \\;=\\; I \\oplus \\tilde{O}(G).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/main-theorem.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"2.4.3"}
